Z||000000||la9||01-28-2000||12:25 PM||||Didn't find much from past threads so I was wondering if anyone knows how the V6 runs without a catalytic converter ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||dogtired||01-28-2000||12:52 PM||||The only way I have to measure it, is by my SEAT - OF - THE - PANTS - METER   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And these are tough to get calibrated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Both my V6s have dead Cats. My 87 was replaced with a straight, 21 inch long piece of pipe. My 86, we gutted the cat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I am not sure one can feel any preformance difference??? But they sure sound GREAT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> No Smog tests here in Kansas, Yet???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||kornholio||01-28-2000||02:36 PM||||I bought my car with no cat convertor.  I put one back on and didn't notice any loss in power.  The car is just a little quieter.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||01-28-2000||04:00 PM||||i have run my car on the Dyno with and with out the cat.. with ot sounds MUCH cooler however! I lost 4lb-tq at the wheels and 3hp by taking the cat off... Go order a Ramdom Cat (2.25 or 2.5" in/out) weld it on.. a straight pipe is nice but the stock motor seems to respond better with the added back pressure. You can get this cat or one similar to it from Summit racing, Random Technologies, and Engineered Performance <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>    oh yeah test done on a 86 V6 4spd.  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 01-28-2000).]||||reg||1
